skill: "oss-license-risk-audit"
sections[3]:
  - "# oss-license-risk-audit\n\nAudit the dependency tree for license risk: build the compatibility matrix, find copyleft paths into proprietary code, and issue the license gate verdict. Use on every release train, when a new dependency is proposed, or when the CI SBOM job flags a new license class. This skill is the enforcement brain behind the legal license gate.\n\nOwner: role-ip-patent-attorney (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"CI SBOM artifact from scripts/generate_sbom.py (package, version, license, dependency edges); project license policy oss-policy.toon (allowed, review, forbidden); module linking model (which modules link or import which)\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/license-audit.toon with compatibility matrix, contamination_paths[], policy exceptions; gate-verdict.toon PASS|BLOCK with evidence\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Read the SBOM artifact from the CI run; an SBOM older than the release candidate commit is stale and blocks the audit with the commit ids named.\n2. Map every package to its license identifier (SPDX where declared); packages with no detectable license go to the review list, never silently to allowed.\n3. Build the compatibility matrix: each license class against the project's distribution model (proprietary, copyleft-linked, SaaS-only) per oss-policy.toon.\n4. Trace contamination paths with run_command over the dependency edges: any path where a strong-copyleft package is linked into a distributed proprietary module; SaaS-only use is recorded as a different, lower risk class per policy.\n5. For each path, collect the evidence chain (package, importer module, distribution surface) - a BLOCK verdict without a traced path is not a verdict, it is a guess.\n6. Check the exception register: previously approved exceptions apply to the same package and use class only, with their approval reference cited.\n7. Issue the verdict: BLOCK when any unexcepted forbidden-class path exists; PASS-WITH-REVIEW when review-class licenses appear without approvals; PASS otherwise.\n8. Write license-audit.toon and gate-verdict.toon; emit the license-clearance handoff to role-staff-engineer and role-general-counsel so the merge gate and the legal record see the same evidence.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ngate verdict to merge gate (council CI) and license-clearance handoff to role-general-counsel.\n"
